# 04_meditation_theta.ledc — Theta Dive (~20 min) — alpha 10 -> theta 6 hold -> return to alert
# Technique: playbook §C arc B "Theta Dive". Alpha induction, slope-limited descent
#            10->6 Hz at 0.5 Hz/min, a 6-min flat theta hold using a DUAL-FREQUENCY
#            L/R offset (left 6.0 Hz / right 6.3 Hz — the ~0.3 Hz offset deepens the
#            state, playbook §C), then a return to alpha so the meditator emerges
#            calm-ALERT (not asleep).
# Bands: induction alpha 10 Hz -> descent 10->6 Hz -> theta hold L6.0/R6.3 -> return alpha 10 Hz.
#
# SAFETY / CONTRAINDICATIONS:
#   Do NOT use if you have photosensitive epilepsy, a seizure disorder, or a history of
#   photic migraine. Do not use while driving. Experiential, not medical.
#   Every rate <=10 Hz (below the 15-25 Hz photosensitive band); binaural carriers 250 Hz
#   (<1000); L/R beat <=10 Hz (<35); brightness capped <=30% with a 10% floor; light ramps
#   in 15 s and fades out over the final 60 s (both >=10 s); blue/violet only (no red).
#
# Driver: TWO binaural channels, freq_r FIXED at 260 Hz on both (freq_r NOT interpolatable).
#   ch1 (panned left  -30): carrier 250->254 => beat 10->6.0 Hz.
#   ch2 (panned right +30): carrier 250->253.7 => beat 10->6.3 Hz (the deepening offset).
#   Beat = freq_r - carrier; the carrier shift is an inaudible <4 Hz move.
# LED: dim violet flicker tracks the mid beat 1:1 (all <=10 Hz), breathing LFO (sine
#   10<->30% / 10 s), four zones (mask 15).
# Ramp convention = animate-on-start (the > prefix sits where a segment BEGINS).

# --- Induction (00:00-01:00, beat 10 Hz): vol + light fade in ---
0 10 50 >0 90 0 200 5            # LED 10 Hz violet flicker, brightness ramps 0->20% over 15 s
A 0 250 -30 >0 0 1 260 0          # ch1 (left)  carrier 250 / R260 = 10 Hz beat; vol fades 0->50
A 0 250 30 >0 0 2 260 0           # ch2 (right) carrier 250 / R260 = 10 Hz beat; vol fades 0->50
S 3000 default 65 "Beginning at ten hertz. Let the alpha rhythm settle you into a calm, easy stillness."
15000 10 50 20 90 0 200 5        # brightness reaches 20% (ramp-in >=10 s done)
30000 10 50 ~10:30:10000 90 0 200 5   # breathing LFO engages: brightness sine 10<->30% over 10 s
A 45000 250 -30 100 0 1 260 0      # ch1 vol settled 50
A 45000 250 30 100 0 2 260 0       # ch2 vol settled 50

# --- Descent to theta (01:00-09:00, beat 10->6 Hz at 0.5 Hz/min) ---
60000 >10 50 ~10:30:10000 90 0 200 5  # LED flicker tracks beat 10->6, breathing LFO continues
A 60000 >250 -30 100 0 1 260 0     # ch1 carrier 250->254 => beat 10->6.0 over 8 min (0.5 Hz/min)
A 60000 >250 30 100 0 2 260 0      # ch2 carrier 250->253.7 => beat 10->6.3 over 8 min
S 60000 default 65 "Drifting down now, descending gently toward theta."

# --- Theta hold: flat 6-min dwell (09:00-15:00, L6.0 / R6.3) ---
540000 6 50 ~10:30:10000 60 0 180 5   # deep violet-blue, LED 6 Hz, breathing LFO
A 540000 254 -30 100 0 1 260 0     # ch1 carrier 254 => beat 6.0 Hz held flat
A 540000 253.7 30 100 0 2 260 0    # ch2 carrier 253.7 => beat 6.3 Hz held flat (0.3 Hz deepening offset)
S 540000 default 65 "You have reached theta, six hertz. Rest here, quiet, open and aware."

# --- Return to alpha (15:00-19:00, beat 6->10 Hz): emerge calm-alert ---
900000 >6 50 ~10:30:10000 60 0 180 5  # LED 6->10 lockstep
A 900000 >254 -30 100 0 1 260 0    # ch1 carrier 254->250 => beat 6.0->10 over 4 min
A 900000 >253.7 30 100 0 2 260 0   # ch2 carrier 253.7->250 => beat 6.3->10 over 4 min
S 900000 default 65 "Slowly rising now, returning toward alpha, clear and refreshed."

# --- Soft close (19:00-20:00): vol + brightness fade to 0 over 60 s ---
1140000 10 50 >20 90 0 200 5     # back to violet; brightness fades 20->0 (>=10 s), preempts LFO
A 1140000 250 -30 >100 0 1 260 0   # ch1 beat back at alpha 10 Hz; vol 50->0
A 1140000 250 30 >100 0 2 260 0    # ch2 beat back at alpha 10 Hz; vol 50->0
S 1140000 default 65 "Back at ten hertz. Gently return to the room, calm and alert."
1200000 10 50 0 90 0 200 5       # end: brightness 0
A 1200000 250 -30 0 0 1 260 0     # end: ch1 volume 0
A 1200000 250 30 0 0 2 260 0      # end: ch2 volume 0
